          "id": "sec-operational-hypothesis-testing-on-discrete-grids",
          "title": "Operational Hypothesis Testing on Discrete Grids",
          "contentAsciiDoc": "== Operational Hypothesis Testing on Discrete Grids\n\n[#theorem-operational-hypothesis-testing]\n[THEOREM]\n.Theorem: Operational Exactness of Discrete Hypothesis Testing\n====\nLet \\( H _ 0 \\) and \\( H _ 1 \\) be operational hypotheses defined on discrete partition grid \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\). The conventional likelihood ratio test statistic \\( \\Lambda ( X ) = \\frac { P ( X \\mid H _ 0 ) } { P ( X \\mid H _ 1 ) } \\) is strictly equivalent to a multivector gauge projection \\( Q _ { \\text { gauge } } ( X ) \\in Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\), wherein conventional \\( p \\)-values represent exact discrete tail-counting aperture fractions under Jaynesian MaxEnt state assignments without continuous integral approximations.\n\n*Proof:*\n\n. **Discrete Tail-Counting Measure**: On finite grid \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\), the operational probability of observing a sample \\( X \\) at least as extreme as \\( x _ 0 \\) under \\( H _ 0 \\) is the finite sum \\( p _ { \\text { tail } } = \\sum _ { x \\in \\mathcal { G } _ N : \\Lambda ( x ) \\le \\Lambda ( x _ 0 ) } P ( x \\mid H _ 0 ) \\mathbf { 1 } _ { Cl } \\).\n\n. **Exact Vernier Bounding**: Because \\( \\mathcal { G } _ N \\) contains a finite step count \\( N \\), \\( p _ { \\text { tail } } \\) is an exact rational step fraction in \\( \\mathbb { R } _ { \\mathcal { I } } \\), avoiding continuum normal or \\( t \\)-distribution approximations.\n\n. **Multivector Likelihood Ratio**: Expressing \\( P ( X \\mid H _ k ) \\) in \\( Cl ( 4 , 1 , 1 ) \\) via Main Scale Projection \\( ( \\downarrow ) \\) yields \\( \\Lambda ( X ) \\) as a scalar blade component of the Jaynesian density tensor.\n\n. **Tautological Conclusion**: Conventional hypothesis testing is an exact finite-aperture tail-counting operation on discrete partition state spaces. \\( \\square \\)\n===="
